From 880052eb1f8a011c261bf9b78e5664229682a524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:50:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] storage: add optional libmdbx backend behind -dbbackend=mdbx
 flag

Adds an optional libmdbx v0.14.4 storage backend selectable at startup via
-dbbackend=leveldb|mdbx (default: leveldb), allocating the concrete backend
adaptors once during database initialization with zero per-operation config
flag lookups:

- C++ CDBWrapper (src/dbwrapper.{h,cpp}):
  - Introduces polymorphic IDBBackend, IDBBatch, and IDBIterator interfaces
    implemented by LevelDBBackend and MdbxBackend.
  - Allocates the chosen backend adaptor once in CDBWrapper::CDBWrapper()
    based on DBParams::backend / GetDefaultDBBackend().
  - Automatically migrates existing node databases in-place on startup if
    switching between -dbbackend=leveldb and -dbbackend=mdbx.
- Rust Chronik (chronik-db, chronik-indexer, chronik-lib):
  - Retains RocksDB as the default backend and allocates either
    DbBackendInstance::Rocks or DbBackendInstance::Mdbx once in Db::open().
  - Uses native MDBX_DUPSORT | MDBX_DUPFIXED tables and custom C batch FFI
    helpers (src/libmdbx/mdbx_batch.{h,c}) when running with -dbbackend=mdbx.
  - Automatically wipes and resyncs indexes/chronik when switching backends.
